- op: discuss  # ae24
  at: '2026-09-19T20:37:05Z'  # ae24
  by: agent  # ae24
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ae24
  clock: 5  # ae24
  nonce: ae24  # ae24
  message: "Satisfied, on the re-scoped statement, with positive evidence measured on both recorded producer fixtures.\n\nTHE CURE'S SHAPE was the owner's call on 2026-09-19 (the row asked for it): the producer declares what it observes, rather than the IR gaining a tri-state. Both would produce the same table; the declaration is contained to the merge/registry layer, where ADR-0057 lives, and does not move a schema promise.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED.\n1. `merge_producers.ABSTENTION_BLIND_ATTRIBUTES` is DERIVED from `Symbol`'s own field defaults over TRACKED_ATTRIBUTES — the tracked attributes whose default is not `None`/`\"\"`/`[]`. It is exactly `(\"is_exported\",)` today. Derived, not listed, so a tracked attribute that gains a concrete default appears there the day it is added.\n2. `MergeAnchor` gains `observes`: of those attributes, the ones this backend computes. `None` means the backend has NOT ruled — the merge pass then takes no candidate from it, and the live-registry contract test refuses any anchored producer of a shared language that left it so. Declaring an attribute that DOES express absence by value is refused at construction, because the record already says that per record and a declaration could only lose it.\n3. `_candidates` consults the declaration for those attributes and only those. For the other nine the value still decides, per record, which is strictly better information.\n4. Declared: `rust` and `python` compute exportedness (`\"pub\" in modifiers`; `__all__` plus the underscore convention) — `observes=(\"is_exported\",)`. `rust_analyzer` and `scip_python` compute none — `observes=()`, verified by grep: neither translation assigns the field anywhere.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE — the phantom is gone and nothing else moved.\n- Recorded aardvark-dns (ADR-0057 §12), `is_exported`: was (107 agree, 41 disagree, 0, 0); now (0, 0, 148 one-sided to `rust`, 0). Every other attribute row is byte-identical: docstring (0,0,63,0), kind (133,15,0,0), modifiers (0,0,35,0), name (83,65,0,0), qualified_name (0,0,148,0), signature (0,0,125,0), span (2,146,0,0), stable_id (0,134,0,14). Pairing, edge overlap, corroborated and superseded counts unchanged.\n- Recorded scip-python sample, `is_exported`: was (4, 6, 0, 0); now (0, 0, 10 one-sided to `python`, 0). Every other row unchanged.\n- No CARRIED value changed anywhere — only the provenance the artifact claims for it. That is the point: the merged record always held the right boolean; the artifact was claiming a second producer had seen it.\n- `docs/audits/0019` regenerated: the `is_exported` row is the only line that moved.\n\nUNIT EVIDENCE, mutation-checked (four mutants, each killed with a real `passed|failed` line):\n- remove the declaration filter from `_candidates` (the defect as filed) -> 2 failed;\n- widen the construction-time validator to accept any tracked attribute -> 1 failed;\n- leave `rust_analyzer`'s `observes` unset -> 2 failed (the contract test, by name);\n- make `rust` wrongly declare it observes nothing -> 2 failed (the fixture tallies).\nThe two behavioural tests pin both halves: an undeclared producer's default does not CONTEST a measured value, and it does not manufacture an AGREEMENT either — the subtler half, where 107 of the 148 records read as two producers concurring.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED rather than swept in (the owner's standing rule):\n- INV-kubup — the same defect one level out, in the ARTIFACT: `Symbol.is_exported: bool = False` means every analyzer with no exportedness rule emits `is_exported: false` as a positive claim, which finalize's fold entrenches and the WI-zimum dead-code seed set reads. Cure is the tri-state the owner weighed and deferred; it is schema-visible.\n- INV-nudoj — `Edge.confidence` (0.85) and `Edge.evidence_type` are concrete defaults arbitrated by the same code path, unaudited. No demonstrated instance (an edge folds only when both producers emitted it), but \"every emitter sets it\" is a claim about emitters, not a property of the type.\n\nCoverage: the two changed core modules are 100% from `hypergumbo-core`'s own tests in isolation; the full 611-file affected slice passes."  # ae24
